format session-log-v1
stamp 20260906.204809
editor Claude Code, Zed-class CLI on the pier
provider Anthropic
product Claude Code
role incense seat -- law, active-designing, iterative review, the captain's hat
modality text
model claude-opus-5
model_status active runtime reported by the harness environment block
voice Kyri
host Linux pier, 8 vCPU / 16 GB, TZ America/New_York
title The fleet set down for a key change
prompt Keaton: can we stop the fleet so I can change Claude Code accounts, then restart kg all after.
think Order first: the watcher before the ships, or it re-arms each one I stop. Sentinel then interrupt then an ANCHORED pkill -- never the bare filename, which cost two ships this morning when a lap's argv carried the baton naming that very file.
think Then the honest report of what the ships are holding, rather than a bare down count. Three trees clean, four dirty, and four carrying a finished signed commit apiece that never reached a remote.
obs I TRIED TO PUBLISH THE FOUR STRANDED COMMITS AND EVERY ONE REFUSED THE FAST-FORWARD. Upstream moved past them while they worked -- my own seven commits today plus their peers'. That is not a loss and not mine to repair: round-open classifies a diverged line, parks it on pier/diverged-STAMP, pushes the park, and adopts the anointed order. The work is preserved BY NAME on relaunch. Rebasing four peers' trees from this seat would be the one-writer law broken in the safest-looking direction.
obs EVERY CREDENTIAL READS 509 BYTES RIGHT NOW, WHICH IS A LIVE TOKEN. After the account change they become 509 bytes of the WRONG account until each tree re-seeds, and agent-jail seeds a tree from the host's when the host's is live and newer -- so the login must land on the host BEFORE the ships relaunch, and the newer mtime is what makes the seeding happen. That ordering is the whole operational point of this stop.
obs THE SENTINEL STAYS ON DISK ON PURPOSE. .watch-stop is what keeps the watcher from respawning inside its own while-loop; the relaunch line removes it. A stop that depends on nobody typing the wrong thing is not a stop.
loom fleet ships_down=7 watcher_down=1 live_agents=0 jailed=0
loom trees dirty=4 clean=3 stranded_commits=4 ff_safe=0
file session-logs/date/20260906/20260906-204809_the-fleet-set-down-for-a-key-change.kyri the record of the set-down and the relaunch order
scope the fleet set down cleanly for an account change, with what each ship holds named
status GREEN -- nothing mid-lap, nothing jailed, no work lost; four diverged lines will park by name on relaunch
recommend check in (Keaton) -- the login is yours to make on the host; the relaunch lines are in the reply and want the host credential live first.
